      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aside: This potentially copies a lot of unnecessary padding, but that seems to have already been the case.\n\nWonder if it would be useful to pack the data tighter when copying it into shared memory, if there\u0027s more than a certain amount of padding. (Dawn native already repacks the memory, or at least it can, if the input alignments are not compatible with the GPU. If we did repacking in the wire client, then we could avoid doing it in Dawn native, so it might even be strictly better.)",
      "revId": "b1f0fd203b6229c101b588d1451959a02d63865f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
